{"reason": "The baseline validation Recall@10 plateaued at 0.83486 because it treats tracker prediction as 355 independent pointwise binary classification targets, neglecting tracker metadata, ecosystem co-occurrence bundles, and domain geographic base rates. Focusing on feature engineering, model design, and training evaluation directly addresses these root causes by injecting empirical Bayes conditional priors, enabling relational tracker self-attention with metadata conditioning, and directly optimizing top-10 ranking discrimination. Historical successful experiments confirm that tracker relational embeddings with metadata conditioning and listwise or margin ranking objectives achieve superior recall well above 0.86.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Compute empirical Bayes smoothed conditional tracker distributions P(tracker|TLD) and P(tracker|category) strictly on train_domain_ids using Dirichlet-multinomial smoothing (alpha=50) to generate a 355-dimensional conditional prior logit vector for each domain, while extracting tracker metadata tensors (company, country, category, brand) from trackers.tsv. WHY: Web tracking is heavily partitioned by legal geography (e.g., GDPR in EU vs. RU/CN ecosystems) and site purpose, which baseline summary features failed to exploit; smoothed priors provide high-confidence baselines so neural capacity focuses on domain-specific residuals. HOW: Aggregate training co-occurrences of tracker_id conditioned on TLD and URL categories, calculate log-odds prior vectors z_prior for train, val, and test splits, and format tracker metadata as categorical index tensors. Interface constraints: Maintain X_train_tensor, X_val_tensor, X_test_tensor, y_train_tensor, y_val_tensor, and feature_columns names and types for compatibility.", "model_design": "WHAT: Upgrade the model to a Tracker-Aware Dual-Encoder network featuring categorical metadata embeddings (company, category, country, brand), multi-head relational self-attention across the 355 trackers, a dynamic residual shortcut for the empirical Bayes prior logits, and a composite Asymmetric plus Top-K Margin Ranking Loss. WHY: Pointwise classification ignores multi-tracker syndication bundles (e.g., Google or Yandex suites) and treats negative classes uniformly rather than penalizing false positives that occupy top-10 prediction slots. HOW: Combine learned tracker embeddings with projected metadata embeddings, process them through multi-head self-attention to form relational tracker representations, compute logits via bilinear dot-product with domain embeddings, add the prior logits shortcut, and compute ranking loss over the hardest top-K negative candidates. Interface constraints: Retain model forward signature and criterion(logits, targets) signature compatible with training and evaluation loops.", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Implement a two-phase dynamic loss weighting schedule where training begins with Asymmetric Loss for probability calibration and progressively ramps up the Top-K margin ranking penalty weight, trained with AdamW and cosine learning rate annealing. WHY: Optimizing hard margin ranking objectives from scratch can destabilize random embeddings; a phased warm-up ensures stable global latent representations before forcing sharp separation around the top-10 decision boundary. HOW: Train for 6 to 8 epochs with batch size 4096 and gradient clipping at 5.0, evaluate exact Recall@10 on the 25,000 holdout domains after each epoch, save and restore the best checkpoint, and generate final test predictions formatted as top-10 tracking_domain_ids per domain in submission/submission.csv and submission.tsv. Interface constraints: Preserve evaluate_recall_at_10, df_submission schema (columns: domain_id, tracking_domain_id), and exact submission file paths."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
