n, outbound diffusion, and direct links, and incorporating a residual Multi-Label Co-occurrence Transition Layer (ML-CTL). WHY: Individual trackers exhibit vastly different link reliabilities (e.g., direct hyperlinks to ad endpoints are near-deterministic whereas inbound diffusion varies widely across tracker types), and primary trackers strongly imply companion trackers within commercial bundles that standard bilinear dot-products miss. HOW: Parameterize in_scale, out_scale, and direct_scale as nn.Parameter(torch.ones(num_trackers)), initialize the ML-CTL transition matrix using empirical conditional co-occurrence probabilities P(tracker_j | tracker_k), and apply a residual refinement step logits = logits + alpha * F.linear(torch.sigmoid(logits), transition_matrix). Interface constraints: Retain the GBTrackerNet forward signature accepting x, in_diff, out_diff, direct_links and returning logit tensors of shape (batch_size, 355).", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Upgrade AsymmetricRecallRankingLoss with a Smooth Top-15 Truncated Ranking Loss aligned directly with Recall@10, maintaining AdamW optimization with OneCycleLR cosine scheduling across the expanded dataset. WHY: Computing LogSumExp across all ~345 negative trackers introduces artificial penalty mass on distant negatives; constraining the negative competition pool to the top-15 hardest negatives per domain focuses gradient updates strictly on the decision threshold governing Recall@10. HOW: In AsymmetricRecallRankingLoss, replace the full negative LogSumExp with torch.topk(neg_logits, k=15, dim=-1).values prior to computing logsumexp and softplus ranking margin penalties, while training for 12 epochs with batch size 1024. Interface constraints: Preserve compute_recall_at_10, build_optimizer_and_scheduler, checkpoint persistence at ./working/best_gb_trackernet.pt, and output formatting for ./submission/submission.csv and ./submission/submission.tsv."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
