tld_prior_train, tld_prior_val, and tld_prior_test as dense float32 arrays of shape (N, 355).", "model_design": "WHAT: Replace the shared single-gate prior summation in GBTrackerNet with a 4-channel Multi-Source Gated Prior Fusion module that assigns independent domain-conditioned gating networks and learnable 355-dimensional scaling vectors to direct hyperlinks, inbound diffusion, outbound diffusion, and 355-dimensional TLD priors. WHY: Direct hyperlinks provide near-deterministic evidence, directional diffusion channels have distinct signal-to-noise ratios, and TLD priors provide vital inductive bias for cold-start domains; a single shared gate forces suboptimal trade-offs across these fundamentally distinct signals. HOW: Parameterize separate scaling vectors (direct_scale, out_scale, in_scale, tld_scale) and separate gating MLPs (Linear(embed_dim, 64) -> SiLU -> Linear(64, num_trackers) -> Sigmoid) for each evidence channel, summing each gated component into domain-tracker bilinear logits before residual ML-CTL co-occurrence refinement. Interface constraints: Update GBTrackerNet forward signature to accept optional tld_prior=None alongside x, in_diff, out_diff, and direct_links while preserving output logit shape (batch_size, 355).", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Upgrade AsymmetricRecallRankingLoss to a Soft Rank-10 Boundary Margin Ranking Loss that computes the smooth rank of each true tracker against negatives and penalizes predictions where the estimated rank exceeds the top-10 threshold. WHY: Recall@10 only cares whether true trackers appear within the top 10 positions; the previous LogSumExp top-15 loss was dominated by the maximum negative logit, causing gradient saturation on top-1 negative separation while validation Recall@10 stalled at 0.8895. HOW: For each domain and positive tracker p, compute soft negative rank as the sum of sigmoid((neg_logits - pos_logit_p) / tau), apply softplus(soft_rank - (10.0 - margin)) / tau, average across positive trackers, and combine with Asymmetric Focal Loss while maintaining OneCycleLR schedule (max_lr=1.2e-3, 12 epochs) and batch size 1024. Interface constraints: Retain compute_recall_at_10, build_optimizer_and_scheduler, model checkpoint persistence at ./working/best_gb_trackernet.pt, and submission generation writing top-10 candidate tracking_domain_ids to ./submission/submission.csv and ./submission/submission.tsv."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
