{"reason": "Validation Recall@10 stalled at 0.8895 because treating hostnames in isolation discards shared organizational tracking stacks across subdomains, while multiplying raw graph diffusion matrices by ITF artificially suppresses ubiquitous trackers like Google Analytics by ~10x relative to rare trackers. Historical experiments confirm that uncorrupted empirical probabilities and dedicated prior channels prevent gradient saturation and plateauing. Data processing, model architecture, and training loops are the exact components to extract root-domain priors, decouple diffusion probabilities from ITF, and integrate a dedicated entity gating head into GBTrackerNet.", "module": ["data_processing_and_feature_engineering", "model_design", "training_evaluation"], "plan": {"data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "WHAT: Extract registered root-domain (SLD.TLD) entities for all hostnames, compute empirical Dirichlet-smoothed 355-dimensional root-domain tracker prior matrices (root_prior_train, root_prior_val, root_prior_test) from training split labels, and decouple raw neighbor diffusion matrices from ITF scaling so diff_in and diff_out retain true empirical probabilities in [0, 1]. WHY: Subdomains under the same parent domain (e.g., store.brand.com and blog.brand.com) deploy near-identical tracking suites, which isolated-hostname processing discards; furthermore, multiplying diff_in and diff_out by ITF severely deflated the additive logits of ubiquitous trackers while amplifying rare tracker noise. HOW: Enhance extract_tld_and_sld to return the registered root domain (handling multi-part suffixes like co.uk and com.au), aggregate tracker frequencies per root entity smoothed by global priors across the 500k training sample, generate root_prior CSR matrices, and in process_directional_diffusion apply ITF scaling solely to SVD decomposition while returning unscaled norm_mat for diffusion priors. Interface constraints: Preserve the shapes and column alignment of X_train, X_val, X_test, maintain diff_in_*, diff_out_*, and direct_* sparse matrix formats, and export root_prior_*.npz to ./working/.", "model_design": "WHAT: Upgrade GBTrackerNet with a dedicated Root-Domain Entity Gating channel featuring a learnable 355-dimensional parameter root_scale and a domain-conditioned gating MLP (Linear(embed_dim, 64) -> SiLU -> Linear(64, num_trackers) -> Sigmoid), adding root_gate * (root_prior * root_scale) directly into domain-tracker logits before ML-CTL refinement. WHY: Organizational root lineage is an authoritative inductive bias distinct from hyperlink topology; giving root-domain priors an independent gating subnetwork prevents interference with graph diffusion channels and enables dynamic soft-activation only when root-level tracking evidence exists. HOW: In GBTrackerNet.__init__, instantiate root_scale as nn.Parameter(torch.ones(num_trackers)) and root_gate as nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(embed_dim, 64), nn.SiLU(), nn.Linear(64, num_trackers), nn.Sigmoid()), and update forward(x, in_diff=None, out_diff=None, direct_links=None, root_prior=None) to inject root_gate(h_domain) * (root_prior * self.root_scale) alongside graph priors into bilinear logits. Interface constraints: Preserve ResidualGatedBlock, TrackerRelationalEmbedding, ML-CTL transition refinement, and AsymmetricRecallRankingLoss untouched, maintaining forward signature compatibility with optional prior arguments.", "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Update batch data collation, training iterations, validation evaluation passes, and final test prediction loops to pass root_prior tensors into GBTrackerNet alongside directional diffusion and direct link tensors. WHY: The empirical root-domain entity prior must be transferred to the GPU in matching mini-batch slices across training, validation, and final 50,000 target domain inference to realize Recall@10 improvements. HOW: Load root_prior_train, root_prior_val, and root_prior_test CSR matrices, slice batch tensors broot_train, broot_val, and broot_test via .toarray() on device, pass root_prior=broot_* to model forward calls, and retain OneCycleLR schedule (12 epochs, max_lr=1.2e-3), best checkpoint restoration, and submission export to ./submission/submission.csv and ./submission/submission.tsv. Interface constraints: Retain compute_recall_at_10, build_optimizer_and_scheduler, best model saving at ./working/best_gb_trackernet.pt, and submission column schema ('domain_id', 'tracking_domain_id')."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
